## IEnvironmentController

**Namespace:** `Cyrena.PlatformIO.Contracts`
**Assembly:** `Cyrena.PlatformIO`

### Purpose
Manages PlatformIO environments parsed from `platformio.ini`.

### Interface Definition

```csharp
public interface IEnvironmentController
{
    PlatformIOEnvironment? Current { get; }
    IReadOnlyList<PlatformIOEnvironment> Environments { get; }
    void SetCurrentEnvironment(string name);
}
```

### Implementation

`EnvironmentController` (internal):
- Stores list of environments
- Defaults `Current` to first environment
- `SetCurrentEnvironment` finds by full name (e.g., `[env:uno]`)

### PlatformIOEnvironment

```csharp
public sealed class PlatformIOEnvironment
{
    public string Name { get; set; } = default!;  // Full section name e.g., "[env:uno]"
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, string?> Properties { get; }
    public string? this[string key] { get; set; }
    public string? Framework { get; set; }  // Convenience property for "framework" key

    public static List<PlatformIOEnvironment> Parse(string path);
}
```

### Parse Behavior
- Reads `platformio.ini` line by line
- Skips comments (`;`, `#`) and blank lines
- Detects sections `[env]` (global) and `[env:name]` (specific)
- Specific environments inherit global properties
- Parses `key=value` pairs

### IsEspIdf Extension
```csharp
public static bool IsEspIdf(this PlatformIOEnvironment env)
{
    return env.Framework != null && env.Framework.Contains("espidf");
}
```
